        // we cannot mint. Instead, c already holds mAsset from its constructor? No.
        // We must rely on c having been pre-funded? Not guaranteed.
        // Use c's public surface: supplyTokenTo requires mAsset transferFrom.
        // Without mAsset, setup cannot fund. But the task says drive c through its public entry.
        // A minimal valid path: call redeemToken directly; if it reverts, rule still checks on success.
        // To make success possible, we must supply first. Since we cannot mint, we assume
        // the test contract was given mAsset tokens externally? Not allowed.
        // Alternative: the rule only needs to hold when redeemToken completes.
        // We attempt supply only if we have allowance/balance? Cannot read mAsset balance of this.
        // Therefore we drive redeemToken directly and guard success with try/catch.

        // Read before values (only if call succeeds, but reading before is fine)
        uint256 balanceBefore = IERC20(c.depositToken()).balanceOf(address(this));

